content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-113, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22650. The motor was replaced yesterday by the electrical contractor; the reported vibration and temperature conditions have occurred since restart.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: the reported 4.8 mm/s at the drive end is above the 2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS Zone B range labelled 'Long-term operation' and within the 4.5–7.1 mm/s RMS Zone C range labelled 'Restricted - plan maintenance'. It is below the 7.1 mm/s Zone C/D boundary and is not in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, Zone D. The applicable measurement basis is vibration velocity in mm/s RMS on bearing housings. Therefore the reported value requires planned maintenance, but does not trigger SSP-07's immediate-stop and reliability-engineer notification rule.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing temperature: the applicable limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C, with bearing temperature measured on the housing surface. The reported housing reading of 70 C is exactly at the upper normal limit, 10 C below alarm and 20 C below trip. It is not above the manufacturer's alarm limit, so SSP-07's rule requiring a priority-1 work order within the shift does not apply to this reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Leakage: no leakage is reported. The evidence gives no numerical allowable-leakage limit for comparison; the troubleshooting table only identifies leakage at the shaft seal as a symptom requiring seal and alignment checks if present. The current report therefore does not, by itself, justify mechanical-seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Planning disposition: P2 is selected to plan and execute the restricted-zone maintenance promptly. Neither documented emergency rule is triggered by the reported readings: vibration is not in Zone D and temperature is not above the 80 C alarm limit. SSP-07 does not otherwise prescribe a Zone C work-order priority or completion deadline.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "First check: shaft misalignment following motor replacement. Misalignment is a documented probable cause of high vibration, and the manual requires laser shaft alignment after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. The timing makes this the leading suspect, but it is not a confirmed diagnosis without alignment measurements.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear remains a documented possible cause. The 70 C housing reading is still within the normal limit and does not independently demonstrate bearing wear or high bearing temperature; bearing condition must be established by inspection if vibration persists.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or impeller damage is another documented possible cause of high vibration; inspect the impeller if alignment correction does not resolve the condition.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation is also a documented possible cause. Check NPSH before attributing persistent vibration solely to mechanical defects; no suction or cavitation evidence is included in the report to rank this cause higher.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Treat the present condition as Zone C planned maintenance. Verify and record the vibration as mm/s RMS on the drive-end bearing housing and reassess it against Figure 3. If any subsequent reading is in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, Zone D, stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. If housing temperature rises above the 80 C alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift; the manufacturer's trip limit is 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Perform laser shaft alignment first because the motor has been replaced. Use a laser alignment tool and bring the installation within the documented tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm. Record as-found and as-left values.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Repeat the vibration assessment after alignment. If high vibration persists, inspect the bearings and impeller and check NPSH to investigate bearing wear, impeller imbalance or damage, and cavitation rather than replacing parts solely on the basis of the initial 4.8 mm/s reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If internal access is required, apply the intrusive-work safety controls, isolate and drain the pump, and use the back pull-out arrangement to remove the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework. Plan the lift for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair: drive-end HF3-512, bearing 6312-C3, and non-drive-end HF3-510, bearing 6310-C3. On reassembly, tighten M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm with lightly oiled threads. The present 70 C reading alone is not above the normal temperature limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not add seal replacement merely because vibration is present when no leakage is reported. If inspection establishes a separate need for seal replacement, follow procedure 5.2: isolate and drain; remove the back pull-out assembly; remove the impeller nut and impeller; withdraw the seal and sleeve; inspect the sleeve; and fit the new seal with a new casing gasket. For serial HF3-22650, fit only pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B, not HF3-450; no sleeve measurement is needed to set this seal. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Tighten the seal gland nuts to 30 Nm. Where the same disassembly requires them, use lightly oiled threads and tighten the M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm and M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "At close-out, document the achieved alignment tolerances and repeat the vibration-zone and housing-temperature assessments. If vibration remains in Zone C, keep the work open for the outstanding bearing, impeller and NPSH diagnosis rather than declaring the repair successful from alignment work alone.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Conditional part: supply with HF3-510 as a pair only if either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Conditional part: supply with HF3-512 as a pair only if bearing replacement is justified by inspection or condition.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal. Conditional part for seal replacement only; it is the mandatory replacement for component seal HF3-450 on this in-scope serial number. Gland-nut torque is 30 Nm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket. Conditional with seal replacement and required whenever the casing is opened; procedure 5.2 requires a new casing gasket with the new seal.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Conditional replacement part: required only if sleeve scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit, draining and venting first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, exceeding SSP-07's 25 kg lifting threshold. Before lifting it, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The current 4.8 mm/s reading is in Zone C and does not require an immediate stop under the highest-zone rule. If vibration enters Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing temperature rises above the manufacturer's 80 C alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift. The documented trip limit is 90 C; the current reading of 70 C activates neither SSP-07 priority rule.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If P-113 is confirmed to be on a chemically dosed line, use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. The supplied chemical-dosing statement specifically identifies P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line, not P-113, so P-113's service must be confirmed rather than assumed.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Initial laser alignment allowance: 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing-replacement allowance, only if the pair must be replaced: 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional mechanical-seal replacement allowance, only if seal replacement is separately justified: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians. Do not add this allowance to the initial alignment-only scope automatically.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal-selection conflict: the manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, but Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, supersedes it for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-113 is serial HF3-22650 and is therefore in scope. For seal work on this asset, use cartridge seal HF3-450B and do not fit HF3-450. The bulletin explicitly leaves HF3-450 and manual Table 5 applicable only to pumps below HF3-22000.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Gland-torque conflict: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014 specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B and identifies 25 Nm as the former value. The serial-specific, later service bulletin governs this asset, so use 30 Nm with HF3-450B. The bulletin does not revise the other Table 5 torques: casing bolts 210 Nm, impeller nut 160 Nm and bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve requirements are supplementary rather than a torque or parts conflict: manual procedure 5.2 requires sleeve inspection but supplies no scoring limit in the provided text. For this in-scope serial, SB-2026-014 supplies the decision criterion: replace HF3-455 when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed for seal setting.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Was the reported 4.8 mm/s measured as RMS on the drive-end bearing housing, as required by Figure 3? The fault report does not explicitly state RMS or the exact measurement point (C07).",
    "Did the electrical contractor perform laser alignment after replacing the motor, and what were the as-found and as-left parallel and angular values? No alignment record is supplied against the 0.05 mm and 0.05 mm per 100 mm tolerances (C10).",
    "What are the bearing inspection/noise findings, impeller condition and suction/NPSH results? These are needed to distinguish the secondary causes. The supplied chunks require inspection and an NPSH check but contain no NPSH acceptance criterion (C09).",
    "What is P-113's line service and pumped fluid, and is that service chemically dosed? C16 identifies chemical dosing only for P-101 to P-106, so it does not establish whether P-113 needs the chemical goggles and nitrile-gloves control in C15 (C15, C16).",
    "What completion deadline is required for the Zone C restriction? Zone C says to plan maintenance, but neither it nor SSP-07 provides a Zone C response time or a P2/P3 priority mapping; the only explicit priority-1 trigger relevant here is temperature above the alarm limit (C07, C15).",
    "No numerical allowable leakage limit or internal seal/sleeve inspection result is supplied. If seal work is proposed, what inspection evidence justifies opening and replacing the seal despite the report of no leakage (C09, C13)?",
    "What labour should be allowed for vibration verification, bearing/impeller inspection and the NPSH check? Table 6 provides standard times only for seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement and laser alignment (C12)."
  ]
}
